- **HIGH — `scripts/land/train.sh:101`, `scripts/push-both.sh:52`, `.githooks/pre-push:33`: publication does not enforce the one-repository destination.** The tools accept arbitrary destination overrides and otherwise trust the name `origin`; the hook checks no destination identity. An unmigrated clone can therefore still publish main to concrete2. Multiple configured push URLs can also publish to multiple repositories through a single `git push origin`, while read-back checks only the fetch destination. `LAND_REPO` can independently select CI evidence from another repository.

  The controls at `scripts/checks/landing_script.sh:650` and `:739` establish command count and ref movement, not repository identity. They pass with arbitrary local destinations. Deferring the remote guard in `changelog.d/2026-11-08-one-repository.md:12` leaves the central migration invariant unenforced; under the requested long-term standard, this is an unfinished structural fix.

  **Long-term fix:** enforce a shared canonical repository identity across publishing tools, the hook and CI queries. Validate every effective push destination, including multiple push URLs and URL rewrites, before publication. Add negative controls for an old-repository origin, fetch/push URL disagreement, multiple push destinations and mismatched CI repository; each must refuse before any ref moves.

The revised documentation correctly distinguishes the owner’s decision from its pending entry in `docs/decisions.md`. I found no language OD selected by this change.

