ROADMAP.md:519:| R-0595 | Heap bounds with the allocation slice (slice 19) ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-memory-2026-11-06)) | when allocation lands, each function reports requested, net and peak logical bytes and footprint per allocator lineage as polynomial bounds with `max`, or "not established"; std containers state per-operation growth bounds; budgets in `Concrete.toml` policies are enforced; "allocation cannot fail" is established only from an allocator success theorem; acceptance examples: a counted push loop into a reserved `Vec` with an exact bound, an arena parser proved infallible, an unbounded `while` giving "not established", branching recursion with only a depth bound giving "not established" for requested bytes, a reset loop accounted by lineage | R-0594, R-0589 |
ROADMAP.md:521:| R-0601 | Function-type contracts, including trait methods (owner, 2026-11-06) | a binding design lets a function whose `#[requires]` is a safety precondition become a function value only under a matching function-type contract; until then such functions are refused as function values, including through wrappers and specialization; it never broadens to non-safety contracts; a prerequisite for accepting slice 20, or earlier if a workload pulls it | R-0571 |
ROADMAP.md:522:| R-0604 | Audit the RocksDB and ethlambda acceptance programs before accepting them (owner, 2026-11-06; revised 2026-11-07) | each program's needs are listed against the decided language; concurrency is now final slice 28, with its model still to be decided, and ethlambda follows it ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-final-slices)); foreign function values (OD4) stay refused, and any real need for them goes to the owner before acceptance; Home: tooling (the audit record). Gate: each program's needs listed against the decided language before acceptance ([tracking](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)) | — |
ROADMAP.md:528:| R-0590 | Delete `legacy/` (LD) once the new compiler implements a full real program ([decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-restart), revised 2026-11-06) | the new compiler implements a full real program such as RocksDB, ethrex or similar (in the slice plan the earliest is the RocksDB acceptance program after slice 25); the sweeps for the areas of C, D and E (R-0591, R-0597, R-0598) have all run, each possibly earlier than its phase, and a final ideas sweep of `legacy/` dispositions every idea (carried, planned, deferred or dropped on purpose); every `RETENTION.tsv` row is resolved; the owner explicitly approves at the time; `legacy/`, the old pipeline included, is then deleted in one change, and the retention records at the root survive it | R-0591, R-0597, R-0598, R-0562, R-0561, owner: approval at the time |
ROADMAP.md:548:| R-0598 | A short ideas sweep of `legacy/` for phase E's area, at the latest at E's start (owner, 2026-11-06) | as R-0591, for E's area, at the latest before E's first item lands (it may run earlier) | R-0591 |
ROADMAP.md:561:| R-0606 | Named assurance properties per module (owner, 2026-11-06) | each property is separate, named and versioned, with its scope, evidence and coverage; there is no ladder of levels | R-0575 |
ROADMAP.md:577:| R-0558 | Move the old tree to `legacy/` in one train and set up the minimal root. Day one, the root holds the README, this file, AGENTS.md, an empty CHANGELOG, LICENSE, the new build files, `ConcreteSpec/Spec.lean`, `docs/PHILOSOPHY.md`, `docs/decisions.md`, the landing, review and hook scripts, `scripts/oracle/`, `required-checks.txt` and its job mapping, `RETENTION.tsv`, the minimal issue record `ISSUES.tsv` with its validator, and the [2026-11 roadmap archive](docs/archive/roadmap-2026-11/README.md) with its task disposition table. Everything else comes back from `legacy/` when a slice needs it. The status page, the work-queue dispatcher, the fuzz farm, perf tracking and the nightly campaign stop, and each is listed in `RETENTION.tsv` as archived; each returns only with a roadmap task. The ci-3 fuzz corpus, perf history and leanprof data were not copied before the handover (decision row P14) and are not archived. | the root holds only that set; a root check refuses any modification or addition under `legacy/`, and any deletion its `RETENTION.tsv` row does not allow (controls for each); no legacy gate runs; the move lands on both remotes | T0, R-0563, R-0565, owner: approval of the move inventory |
