## 1. Inventory: concepts defined more than once

### 1.1 Keyed lookup, update and removal

| Copy | Where |
|---|---|
| `lookupF` (generic) | `Spec/Syntax.lean:23` |
| `envFind` | `Spec/Semantics.lean:62` |
| `ctxFind` (by `Entry.name`) | `Spec/Ownership.lean:35` |
| `Borrow.find` (`Nat` keys, `Place` values) | `Spec/Borrow.lean:42` |
| `Borrow.getN` (`Nat` keys, any value) — the same pattern, polymorphic, in the same file | `Spec/Borrow.lean:404` |
| `Brand.findL` | `Spec/Brand.lean:32` |
| `findDecl`, `Prog.find` (via `List.find?`) | `Spec/Syntax.lean:87`, `Spec/Authority.lean:151` |
| updates: `envMove`, `ctxMark`, `putN`, `mapPlaces` | `Spec/Semantics.lean:67`, `Spec/Ownership.lean:40`, `Spec/Borrow.lean:409,46` |
| removals: `Borrow.remove`, `Brand.removeL` | `Spec/Borrow.lean:48`, `Spec/Brand.lean:36` |
| lemmas proved per copy | `Proofs/Basics.lean:11,20` (`ctxFind_mem`, `lookupF_map`); `Proofs/Borrow.lean:11,21,40,450` (`find_mem` and the `getN`/`putN` lemmas); `Proofs/Brand.lean:11,20,31,372,378`; also `tys_lookup` and `ctxMark_tys` (`Proofs/Slice1.lean`) |

**Unified:** one `AList` API (`lookup`, `update`, `erase`, `map`) in `Spec/Basics.lean`, with its lemmas
once in `Proofs/Basics.lean`. Every map is keyed by a typed identity (1.2).

### 1.2 Identities and sites


The owner may then approve one exact commit (R-0618), after Codex, Kimi and agy have all reviewed
that commit. The cap is the class of the branch's diff against its base, by path, the highest class
present winning: docs and roadmap 2 rounds, scripts 3, compiler and spec 5 (an unclassified path
counts as compiler and spec); it counts the rounds used, whatever their verdicts. The approval is
recorded, from the owner's own words only, with `scripts/land/signoff.sh record <sha> --base <base>
--rounds-at <the review.sh-noted commit> --date --quote`, plus `--codex-request <request> --codex
<output>` and the corresponding kimi and agy options. For each reviewer `r`, the recorder stores the
verbatim request as `r-request.txt` after prepending `reviewed: <sha>`, and the output separately as
`r.txt`. The request body must name that commit by an unambiguous prefix, and only the output's last
verdict line counts; it must be `VERDICT: ACCEPT`. Recording refuses a record that does not qualify.
Push the resulting `refs/owner-signoff/<sha>` to origin. The landing train accepts it as that
commit's review provenance ([LANDING.md](LANDING.md)); it approves no other commit.

## verify.sh

```sh
scripts/review/verify.sh <commit>          # exit 0 clean, 1 findings/blocked, 2 none or malformed
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Fetch the published oracle artifact and install it, verified (ROADMAP R-0564; P13).
#
#   fetch.sh    download artifact_url from the lock, check artifact_sha256, unpack into
#               $ORACLE_HOME/<commit>/ and verify the install (manifest, nothing added, binary hash)
#
# This is how a runner other than concrete-ci-2 (a GitHub-hosted fallback runner) gets the oracle.
# The digest in the lock is what authenticates the download: the bytes are trusted because their
# sha256 is the one the reviewed lock names, whatever served them. build.sh is the independent
# check that those bytes are what the tag builds.
#
# Exit status: 0 installed and verified; 3 INCOMPLETE (no published artifact, download failed, or
# verification failed). A caller reports 3 as incomplete, which blocks landing when the oracle check
# is required; it never reports it as passed and never falls back to an unverified binary.
set -uo pipefail
HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
# shellcheck source=scripts/oracle/lib.sh
. "$HERE/lib.sh"
incomplete() { echo "oracle: INCOMPLETE: $*" >&2; exit 3; }
URL="$(lock artifact_url)"; WANT="$(lock artifact_sha256)"
case "$URL" in https://*) ;; *) incomplete "no published artifact (artifact_url is '${URL:-empty}')";; esac
[ ${#WANT} = 64 ] || incomplete "the lock has no artifact_sha256"
D="$(oracle_home)/$(lock commit)"
if oracle_verify_install "$D" >/dev/null 2>&1; then echo "oracle: already installed and verified at $D"; exit 0; fi
mkdir -p "$(oracle_home)" || incomplete "cannot create $(oracle_home)"
TMPF="$(mktemp "$(oracle_home)/fetch.XXXXXX")" || incomplete "no temporary file"
trap 'rm -f "$TMPF"' EXIT
curl -fsSL --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 --retry 3 -o "$TMPF" "$URL" || incomplete "download of $URL failed"
why="$(oracle_install "$TMPF" "$D")" || incomplete "$why"
echo "oracle: fetched $URL, verified $WANT, installed at $D"

exec
/bin/bash -lc "printf 'gate shell: %s\\n' \""'${CONCRETE_GATES_SHELL:-unset}"; sed -n '"'1,95p' scripts/checks/landing_script.sh; cat scripts/checks/sandbox_isolation.sh; cat scripts/checks/legacy_frozen.sh | tail -38; cat scripts/checks/root_inventory.sh | tail -28; cat scripts/checks/oracle_fetch.sh | head -80" in /tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-b/src
 succeeded in 0ms:
gate shell: unset
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# THE LANDING SCRIPT RESOLVES ONLY WHAT IS MECHANICAL AND REFUSES EVERYTHING ELSE (R-0539).
#
# scripts/land/train.sh builds one integrated candidate from several branches and lands it. The
# hand-run version of that job, on 2026-10-22, made the mistakes this gate pins down: a rebase piped
# to `tail` kept going and a commit was made mid-rebase; union-merged ledgers kept stale entries
# (two OPEN corpus entries for fixed bugs); and candidates were pushed without checking that the CI
# result described them. Each leg below drives the real script against a THROWAWAY repository with
# bare-repo remotes and a fake `gh`, so nothing here can touch this repository, its remotes or CI.
#
#   resolution  generated views (a ROADMAP generated block, a whole generated file) are regenerated,
#               ledgers are union-merged; the train carries both members' entries
#   refusal     a conflict in source or in prose outside a generated block aborts the merge (no
#               MERGE_HEAD left, exit 3); a union that duplicates a corpus key is refused; a
#               merge or rebase already in progress, a dirty tree and an existing train are refused
#   pipeline    check feeds the hook exactly base..head on ci/<name>; ci pushes and records the run
#   watch       a campaign-only failure is reported as such; a landing failure fetches log tails
#   land        refused on a head-SHA mismatch, a red landing job, a moved main, a remote named fork;
#               dry-run pushes nothing; a real land with no lambdaclass remote pushes origin exactly
#               once and no second remote, and cancels no run (main's own run records the train's, R-0570)
#   record      (2026-11-06, R-0570) main's run names the run that qualified its exact SHA only when
#               the newest completed dispatch of the CI workflow at that SHA AND at that base (its
#               title, from the base input train.sh ci passes) passed every landing-tier and required
#               job and the head is ahead of the base; a missing run, a run at another SHA or base, of
#               another workflow or event, unfinished or excluded, a skipped,
#               cancelled or failed job, an older green run behind a newer red one, a diverged or
#               absent base: no record. The workflow gates every job on it (structure check)
#   dropped     (2026-10-25) a push that fails before the remote moved is retried; one that fails
#               after it moved is accepted from ls-remote; exhausted retries fail and move nothing
#   bisect      halving finds a seeded red member
#   report      the median time to land is computed from the log
#   gate host   (2026-11-05) check's impact leg on the gate host: bound to the train head's SHA (a
#               run at another SHA, an unreachable host or a lost log is INCOMPLETE and blocks; only
#               --local-gates runs here); the hook reuses the attestation only for this exact push, and
#               a tampered log or attestation is refused
#   review      (2026-11-06) review fails closed: check with no review command fails; a reviewer that
#               exits 0 but leaves no note, a malformed, blocked or findings note fails the leg; check
#               skips the reviewer when every member is reviewed clean; land requires a clean head
#               note, or (head unreviewed) a clean note on every member, and refuses an absent,
#               malformed, blocked or findings note in either place
#   required    (2026-11-04) a required job (required-checks.txt) that is missing, skipped or
#               cancelled refuses watch and land; a candidate drops a requirement main imposes only
#               through a transition row (replaced by jobs it requires and that pass, or retired with
#               a reason and reported as retired); the file names the workflow's landing-tier jobs
set -uo pipefail
source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/lib/gate_env.sh" || exit 2
ROOT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../.." && pwd)"
TRAIN="$ROOT_DIR/scripts/land/train.sh"
REPORT="$ROOT_DIR/scripts/land/report.sh"
[ -f "$TRAIN" ] && [ -f "$REPORT" ] || { echo "FATAL: scripts/land/train.sh or report.sh missing" >&2; exit 2; }
TMP="$(mktemp -d)" || { echo "FATAL: could not create a sandbox directory" >&2; exit 2; }
[ -n "$TMP" ] && [ -d "$TMP" ] || { echo "FATAL: sandbox directory is not usable" >&2; exit 2; }
trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT
PASS=0; FAIL=0
ok(){ echo "  ok   $1"; PASS=$((PASS+1)); }
no(){ echo "  FAIL $1"; FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); }

# Isolation: no inherited repository (the hook leaks GIT_DIR), no user or system git config (hooks
# path, conflict style, signing), no toolchain re-entry.
source "$ROOT_DIR/scripts/checks/lib/git_sandbox.sh" || exit 2
git_sandbox "$TMP/gitconfig" || exit 2
cat > "$GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL" <<EOF
[user]
	name = landing gate
	email = gate@example.invalid
[init]
	defaultBranch = main
[core]
	hooksPath = $TMP/nohooks
[merge]
	conflictStyle = diff3
EOF
mkdir -p "$TMP/nohooks"
# train.sh runs only with the repository's pre-push hook enabled (ISS-0015): it asks the hook git
# would run who it is (its single argument --concrete-identify). The sandbox's global hooksPath holds this
# stand-in, which runs no gate and answers as the repository's .githooks/pre-push would: a test
# fixture impersonating the hook on purpose.
IDENTIFY='[ "$#" = 1 ] && [ "$1" = --concrete-identify ] && { echo "concrete-pre-push $(cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" && pwd -P)/.githooks/pre-push"; exit 0; }'
standin_hook() {
  printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\n%s\nexit 0\n' "$IDENTIFY" > "$TMP/nohooks/pre-push"
  chmod +x "$TMP/nohooks/pre-push"
}
standin_hook
export LAND_NO_NIX=1 LAND_STATE_DIR="$TMP/state" LAND_GH="$TMP/fake-gh" LAND_REPO=test/repo
export LAND_PUSH_RETRY_SLEEP=0
unset LAND_GATES_HOST LAND_GATES_TRANSPORT CONCRETE_PREPUSH_NO_REUSE
export FAKE_GH_DIR="$TMP/gh"; mkdir -p "$FAKE_GH_DIR"

cat > "$TMP/fake-gh" <<'GH'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# A fake gh: run state comes from $FAKE_GH_DIR, every call is appended to calls.log.
echo "$*" >> "$FAKE_GH_DIR/calls.log"
case "$1 $2" in
  "workflow run") exit 0 ;;
  "run list") cat "$FAKE_GH_DIR/list.json" ;;
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# SANDBOXES NEVER TOUCH THE CALLER'S REPOSITORY (ISS-0015).
#
# A pre-push hook of a linked worktree runs with GIT_DIR=<repo>/.git/worktrees/<name> exported. On
# 2026-11-06 review_tool.sh, run that way, did its sandbox work in the caller's clone and pushed 28 +
# 12 test notes to GitHub. The owner of the fix is the sandbox helper, scripts/checks/lib/
# git_sandbox.sh, which unsets every variable `git rev-parse --local-env-vars` names.
#
# Legs:
#   structural  every script under scripts/ that makes a repository
#               (git init, git clone, git worktree add) sources the helper and calls git_sandbox.
#   live        a throwaway CALLER (bare upstream, full clone, linked worktree; no hook installed
#               anywhere) runs review_tool.sh and legacy_frozen.sh, at this checkout's version, from
#               the linked worktree with GIT_DIR exported exactly as a hook sees it. The caller's
#               refs (refs/notes/* included), core.bare, worktree HEAD and its upstream's refs must be
#               byte-for-byte unchanged.
#   control     the same harness around a script that writes through an inherited GIT_DIR (as the
#               unfixed review_tool.sh did) must report the change, so the live leg cannot pass by
#               not looking.
#
# Every run is bounded in time (120 s per attempt, bounded_run) and in aggregate: a systemd user
# scope with TasksMax=512 and MemoryMax=8G (fede-256gb, concrete-ci-2 logins), or, where there is
# none (a CI runner service), the cgroup the check already runs in when it has a finite memory.max
# (concrete-ci-2's runners: 28G per runner) plus `ulimit -u` of 512 more processes. With neither, the
# live probes do not run and the check fails as INCOMPLETE: never an unbounded run. macOS has
# neither (no unprivileged aggregate memory limit), so there the root checks are INCOMPLETE by design
# and a gated push from a macOS clone is refused: gated pushes (trains) are made from a Linux clone
# with a bound (fede-256gb or concrete-ci-2; no laptop builds), and CI runs on bounded runners. The 2026-11-06
# reproducer had no such bound, recursed through a test hook and exhausted the machine.
set -uo pipefail
source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/lib/gate_env.sh" || exit 2
ROOT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../.." && pwd)"
cd "$ROOT_DIR" || exit 2
HELPER="scripts/checks/lib/git_sandbox.sh"
[ -f "$HELPER" ] || { echo "FATAL: $HELPER missing" >&2; exit 2; }
PASS=0; FAIL=0
ok(){ echo "  ok   $1"; PASS=$((PASS+1)); }
no(){ echo "  FAIL $1"; FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); }

echo "=== structural: every repository-making script sources the sandbox helper ==="
# One exception, not a sandbox: worktree-new.sh makes a worktree OF the caller's repository by design.
EXEMPT=" scripts/worktree-new.sh "
MAKES='git( -C [^ ]+)? (init|clone)\b|worktree add'
# shell_scripts DIR: every shell script under DIR/scripts at ANY depth, as paths relative to DIR,
# sorted: a `*.sh` file, or any other file whose first line is a sh/bash shebang. (Until 2026-11-08
# the scan was `scripts/*.sh scripts/*/*.sh`, so a script two directories down was never looked at.)
shell_scripts() {
  (cd "$1" && find scripts -type f -print | LC_ALL=C sort | while IFS= read -r f; do
    case "$f" in
      *.sh) echo "$f" ;;
      *) head -n 1 "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -qE '^#!.*[/ ](ba)?sh([[:space:]]|$)' && echo "$f" ;;
    esac
  done)
}
# scan_makers DIR: one line per repository-making script under DIR (exemptions and this check
# skipped): `ok<TAB>file<TAB>why` or `FAIL<TAB>file<TAB>why`. The helper must be sourced and
# called, as statements, before the first repository is made.
scan_makers() {
  local dir="$1" f first_make src_line call_line
  shell_scripts "$dir" | while IFS= read -r f; do
    [ "$f" = scripts/checks/sandbox_isolation.sh ] && continue
    case "$EXEMPT" in *" $f "*) continue ;; esac
    grep -qE "$MAKES" "$dir/$f" || continue
    first_make="$(grep -nE "$MAKES" "$dir/$f" | grep -vE '^[0-9]+:[[:space:]]*#' | head -n 1 | cut -d: -f1)"
    src_line="$(grep -nE '^[[:space:]]*(source|\.) .*checks/lib/git_sandbox\.sh' "$dir/$f" | head -n 1 | cut -d: -f1)"
    call_line="$(grep -nE '^[[:space:]]*git_sandbox( |$)' "$dir/$f" | head -n 1 | cut -d: -f1)"
    if [ -n "$src_line" ] && [ -n "$call_line" ] && [ -n "$first_make" ] \
       && [ "$src_line" -lt "$call_line" ] && [ "$call_line" -lt "$first_make" ]; then
      printf 'ok\t%s\tsources git_sandbox.sh (line %s) and calls it (line %s) before its first repository (line %s)\n' "$f" "$src_line" "$call_line" "$first_make"
    else
      printf 'FAIL\t%s\tmakes a repository (line %s) without sourcing (line %s) and calling git_sandbox (line %s) before it\n' "$f" "${first_make:-?}" "${src_line:-none}" "${call_line:-none}"
    fi
  done
}
makers=0
while IFS=$'\t' read -r verdict f why; do
  makers=$((makers+1))
  if [ "$verdict" = ok ]; then ok "$f $why"; else no "$f $why"; fi
done < <(scan_makers "$ROOT_DIR")
[ "$makers" -ge 8 ] && ok "found $makers repository-making scripts (at least the 8 known)" \
  || no "found only $makers repository-making scripts; the scan is not seeing them"

echo "=== control: the structural scan sees scripts at any depth and without a .sh suffix ==="
# A planted tree: an unsandboxed maker three directories down and one with a bash shebang and no
# suffix must both FAIL; a sandboxed one at depth must pass. The scan cannot pass by not looking.
CTL_TREE="$(mktemp -d)" || exit 2
mkdir -p "$CTL_TREE/scripts/a/b/c"
printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\ngit init -q "$1"\n' > "$CTL_TREE/scripts/a/b/c/deep.sh"
printf '#!/bin/bash\ngit clone -q "$1" "$2"\n' > "$CTL_TREE/scripts/a/b/nosuffix"
printf '#!/usr/bin/env bash\nsource "$(dirname "$0")/../../checks/lib/git_sandbox.sh"\ngit_sandbox "$1"\ngit init -q "$2"\n' > "$CTL_TREE/scripts/a/b/good.sh"
ctl="$(scan_makers "$CTL_TREE")"; rm -rf "${CTL_TREE:?}"
printf '%s\n' "$ctl" | grep -q $'^FAIL\tscripts/a/b/c/deep.sh\t' \
  && ok "an unsandboxed maker three directories down is refused" || no "the scan missed scripts/a/b/c/deep.sh: $ctl"
printf '%s\n' "$ctl" | grep -q $'^FAIL\tscripts/a/b/nosuffix\t' \
  && ok "an unsandboxed maker with a bash shebang and no .sh suffix is refused" || no "the scan missed scripts/a/b/nosuffix: $ctl"
printf '%s\n' "$ctl" | grep -q $'^ok\tscripts/a/b/good.sh\t' \
  && ok "a sandboxed maker at depth passes" || no "the scan did not accept scripts/a/b/good.sh: $ctl"

# The harness itself is a sandbox: it must not be steered by whatever environment started it.
source "$HELPER" || exit 2
TMP="$(mktemp -d)" || exit 2
trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT
git_sandbox "$TMP/gitconfig" || exit 2
printf '[user]\n\tname = isolation gate\n\temail = isolation@example.invalid\n[init]\n\tdefaultBranch = main\n[advice]\n\tdetachedHead = false\n' > "$GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL"

BOUNDED_PARENT="$TMP"
source "$ROOT_DIR/scripts/checks/lib/bounded.sh" || exit 2
# bounded <cmd...>: at most 120 s per attempt (the portable bounded_run: its own watchdog kills the
# whole process group; one re-run), inside an aggregate task and memory bound (above). Without one
# the command does not run and the result is 125.
cgroup_memory_max() { # the finite memory.max of this process's cgroup v2 or an ancestor, else fails
  local cg f
  cg="$(sed -n 's/^0:://p' /proc/self/cgroup 2>/dev/null)"; [ -n "$cg" ] || return 1
  while :; do
    f="/sys/fs/cgroup$cg/memory.max"
    if [ -r "$f" ] && [ "$(cat "$f")" != max ]; then cat "$f"; return 0; fi
    [ "$cg" = / ] && return 1
    cg="$(dirname "$cg")"
  done
}
BOUND=none
if command -v systemd-run >/dev/null 2>&1 \
   && systemd-run --user --scope -q -p TasksMax=512 -p MemoryMax=8G true >/dev/null 2>&1; then BOUND=scope
elif CGMEM="$(cgroup_memory_max)"; then BOUND=cgroup; fi
case "$BOUND" in
  scope)  echo "bound: a systemd user scope, TasksMax=512, MemoryMax=8G" ;;
  cgroup) echo "bound: this cgroup's memory.max ($CGMEM bytes, aggregate) and ulimit -u (512 more processes)" ;;
  none)   echo "bound: none available (no systemd user scope, no finite cgroup memory.max; macOS has neither): the live probes will not run; run the root checks and gated pushes from a bounded Linux host (fede-256gb, concrete-ci-2) or in CI" ;;
esac
bounded() {
  case "$BOUND" in
    scope) bounded_run -i /dev/null -r 120 120 -- systemd-run --user --scope -q -p TasksMax=512 -p MemoryMax=8G "$@" ;;
    cgroup)
      local n; n="$(ps -o pid= -U "$(id -u)" 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d ' ')"
      ( ulimit -u $(( ${n:-0} + 512 )) 2>/dev/null || { echo "sandbox_isolation: ulimit -u refused; not running $*"; exit 125; }
        bounded_run -i /dev/null -r 120 120 -- "$@" ) ;;
    *) echo "sandbox_isolation: no aggregate task and memory bound here; not running $*"; return 125 ;;
  esac
}

# A caller: bare upstream, a full clone of this checkout's HEAD, a linked worktree of it, with this
# checkout's scripts/ (the version under test) copied over the worktree's. No hook is installed:
# hooksPath points at an empty directory.
mk_caller() { # dir
  local d="$1"
  mkdir -p "$d/nohooks"
  git clone -q --bare "$ROOT_DIR" "$d/up.git" || return 1
  git clone -q "$d/up.git" "$d/caller" || return 1
  git -C "$d/caller" config core.hooksPath "$d/nohooks"
  git -C "$d/caller" worktree add -q -b isolation-probe "$d/linked" || return 1
  cp -R "$ROOT_DIR/scripts/." "$d/linked/scripts/" || return 1
  git -C "$d/linked" add -A scripts && git -C "$d/linked" commit -q --allow-empty -m "scripts under test" || return 1
}
snap() { # dir
  local d="$1"
  git -C "$d/caller" for-each-ref --format='caller %(refname) %(objectname)'
  echo "caller core.bare=$(git -C "$d/caller" config core.bare)"
  echo "linked HEAD=$(git -C "$d/linked" rev-parse HEAD) $(git -C "$d/linked" symbolic-ref -q HEAD)"
  git -C "$d/caller" worktree list --porcelain | grep '^worktree '
  git -C "$d/up.git" for-each-ref --format='upstream %(refname) %(objectname)'
}
# run_as_hook <dir> <script relative to the linked worktree>: GIT_DIR exported as a linked
# worktree's hook sees it; prints the script's exit code.
run_as_hook() {
  local d="$1" s="$2" gd
  gd="$(git -C "$d/linked" rev-parse --absolute-git-dir)"
  ( cd "$d/linked" && GIT_DIR="$gd" && export GIT_DIR && bounded bash "$s" ) > "$d/run.log" 2>&1
  echo $?
}
probe() { # label script expect-change [completion-marker]
  local label="$1" s="$2" want="$3" marker="${4:-}" d rc
  d="$(mktemp -d "$TMP/caller.XXXXXX")"
  mk_caller "$d" || { no "$label: could not build the caller"; return; }
  [ -z "$(ls "$d/nohooks")" ] || { no "$label: a hook is installed"; return; }
  snap "$d" | LC_ALL=C sort > "$d/before"
  rc="$(run_as_hook "$d" "$s")"
  snap "$d" | LC_ALL=C sort > "$d/after"
  if [ "$want" = 0 ]; then
    [ "$rc" = 125 ] && { no "$label: INCOMPLETE: no task and memory bound available, so it was not run"; return; }
    bounded_is_incomplete "$rc" && { no "$label: INCOMPLETE: timed out twice (120 s each)"; tail -n 5 "$d/run.log" | sed 's/^/      /'; return; }
    [ "$rc" = 0 ] || { no "$label: exit $rc (an early failure would make 'unchanged' vacuous)"; tail -n 8 "$d/run.log" | sed 's/^/      /'; }
    grep -q "$marker" "$d/run.log" || { no "$label: its final tally ('$marker') is missing: it stopped early, so 'unchanged' proves nothing"; return; }
    if cmp -s "$d/before" "$d/after"; then ok "$label: the caller's refs, notes, config and upstream are unchanged"
    else no "$label: the caller changed"; diff "$d/before" "$d/after" | sed 's/^/      /' | head -20; fi
  else
    [ "$rc" = 125 ] && { no "$label: INCOMPLETE: no task and memory bound available, so it was not run"; return; }
    bounded_is_incomplete "$rc" && { no "$label: INCOMPLETE: timed out twice"; return; }
    grep -q 'refs/notes/' "$d/after" && ! cmp -s "$d/before" "$d/after" \
      && ok "$label: the harness sees a write through the inherited GIT_DIR" \
      || no "$label: a leaking script left the caller unchanged; the harness is blind"
  fi
}

echo "=== control: the harness sees a leak ==="
mkdir -p "$TMP/ctl"
cat > "$TMP/ctl/leaky.sh" <<'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# What the unfixed review_tool.sh did: build a sandbox without clearing GIT_DIR, then write to it.
T="$(mktemp -d)"; git init -q "$T/w"
git -C "$T/w" commit -q --allow-empty -m leaked
git -C "$T/w" notes --ref=refs/notes/concrete-review add -m "verdict: clean" HEAD
EOF
probe "control (leaky script)" "$TMP/ctl/leaky.sh" 1

echo "=== live: sandbox checks run from a linked worktree as its hook would run them ==="
probe "review_tool.sh" scripts/checks/review_tool.sh 0 "^check_review_tool: PASS=[0-9]* FAIL=0$"
probe "legacy_frozen.sh" scripts/checks/legacy_frozen.sh 0 "^legacy_frozen: PASS=[0-9]* FAIL=0$"

echo
bounded_summary
echo "check_sandbox_isolation: PASS=$PASS FAIL=$FAIL"
[ "$FAIL" -eq 0 ]
[ -n "$(judge "$F" "$T" "$TMP/r_open.tsv")" ] && ok "control: a deletion under an open row is refused" || no "control: open-row deletion accepted"
[ -n "$(judge "$F" "$T" "$TMP/r_nostatus.tsv")" ] && ok "control: a deletion without a status column is refused" || no "control: status-less deletion accepted"
[ -z "$(judge "$F" "$T" "$TMP/r_ok.tsv")" ] && ok "control: a deletion under a resolved row passes" || no "control: resolved-row deletion refused"
printf 'path\tstatus\nb\tresolved\nb/y\topen\n' > "$TMP/r_child.tsv"
T="$(tree_with 'rm -rf b')"
[ -n "$(judge "$F" "$T" "$TMP/r_child.tsv")" ] && ok "control: a resolved parent does not release a child with an open row" || no "control: open child released by resolved parent"
T="$(tree_with 'rm -f a/x')"
[ -n "$(judge "$F" "$T" "$TMP/r_ok.tsv")" ] && ok "control: a deletion outside the resolved row is refused" || no "control: unrelated deletion accepted"
cd "$ROOT_DIR"

echo "=== legacy/ against $LOCK ==="
[ -f "$LOCK" ] || { no "$LOCK is missing"; echo "legacy_frozen: PASS=$PASS FAIL=$FAIL"; exit 1; }
base="$(sed -n 's/^base //p' "$LOCK")"; frozen="$(sed -n 's/^tree //p' "$LOCK")"
pv="$(sed -n 's/^preview //p' "$LOCK")"
[ -z "$pv" ] && ok "the move was generated with its landing prerequisites met" \
  || no "the move is a --preview build ($pv); regenerate it with scripts/land/legacy_move.sh on a base that meets them"
if [ -z "$base" ] || [ -z "$frozen" ]; then
  no "$LOCK needs a 'base <commit>' and a 'tree <oid>' line"
elif [ "$(git rev-parse -q --verify "$base^{tree}" 2>/dev/null)" != "$frozen" ]; then
  no "the recorded tree $frozen is not the tree of the recorded base $base (or the base is not in this clone's history)"
else
  ok "legacy.lock: tree ${frozen:0:10} is the tree of base ${base:0:10}"
  cur="$(git rev-parse -q --verify HEAD:legacy 2>/dev/null)"
  if [ -z "$cur" ]; then
    no "HEAD has no legacy/ directory"
  else
    [ -f RETENTION.tsv ] || { no "RETENTION.tsv is missing"; }
    out="$(judge "$frozen" "$cur" "${RETENTION:-RETENTION.tsv}" 2>&1)"
    if [ -z "$out" ]; then
      [ "$cur" = "$frozen" ] && ok "legacy/ is byte-identical to the frozen tree" \
                            || ok "legacy/ differs from the frozen tree only by deletions RETENTION.tsv allows"
    else
      no "legacy/ changed:"; echo "$out" | sed 's/^/      /'
    fi
  fi
fi
echo "legacy_frozen: PASS=$PASS FAIL=$FAIL"
[ "$FAIL" -eq 0 ]
want = {l.strip() for l in open(sys.argv[1]) if l.strip() and not l.startswith("#")}
have = set()
for p in (l.rstrip("\n") for l in sys.stdin):
    if not p: continue
    parts = p.split("/")
    have.add(parts[0])
    if parts[0] in ("docs", "scripts") and len(parts) > 1:
        have.add(parts[0] + "/" + parts[1])
for e in sorted(have - want): print("not in the day-one set: " + e)
for e in sorted(want - have): print("listed but missing: " + e)
' "$1"
}

echo "=== negative controls ==="
TMP="$(mktemp -d)" || exit 2
trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT
printf 'a\nb\ndocs\ndocs/x.md\n' > "$TMP/list"
[ -z "$(printf 'a\nb/c\ndocs/x.md\n' | judge "$TMP/list")" ] && ok "control: exactly the listed set passes" || no "control: listed set refused"
[ -n "$(printf 'a\nb/c\ndocs/x.md\nstray\n' | judge "$TMP/list")" ] && ok "control: an unlisted top-level entry is refused" || no "control: stray accepted"
[ -n "$(printf 'a\nb/c\ndocs/x.md\ndocs/y.md\n' | judge "$TMP/list")" ] && ok "control: an unlisted docs/ entry is refused" || no "control: docs stray accepted"
[ -n "$(printf 'a\ndocs/x.md\n' | judge "$TMP/list")" ] && ok "control: a missing listed entry is refused" || no "control: missing accepted"

echo "=== the tracked root against $LIST ==="
[ -f "$LIST" ] || { no "$LIST is missing"; echo "root_inventory: PASS=$PASS FAIL=$FAIL"; exit 1; }
out="$(git ls-files --cached | judge "$LIST")"
[ -z "$out" ] && ok "the root holds exactly the day-one set" || { no "the root differs from the day-one set:"; echo "$out" | sed 's/^/      /'; }
echo "root_inventory: PASS=$PASS FAIL=$FAIL"
[ "$FAIL" -eq 0 ]
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# A RUNNER WITHOUT A VERIFIED ORACLE NEVER PASSES THE ORACLE CHECK (ISS-0005, P13; ROADMAP R-0564).
#
# scripts/oracle/ci_check.sh is the required oracle job on GitHub-hosted runners: fetch.sh downloads
# the published artifact and verifies it, then run.sh runs smoke.con through it. This gate runs the
# real fetch.sh, run.sh and ci_check.sh on a scratch copy of scripts/oracle with a test lock, a test
# artifact built with the real packer (lib.sh oracle_pack) and a fake `curl` (no network), and holds
# them to: a good artifact installs and verifies (positive control); a lock with no published
# artifact, a failed download, an artifact with other bytes, and an artifact whose install fails
# verification (manifest not the locked one) each leave fetch.sh and ci_check.sh INCOMPLETE (exit 3),
# never passed; an installed oracle whose files were altered is refused by run.sh (125) before
# anything runs, and ci_check.sh reports that as INCOMPLETE (an install altered after fetch.sh); a verified oracle whose smoke run exits
# other than 42, a compile failure (whatever its status, 42 included) and a compile that writes no
# program are FAILED (1), through the real run.sh with a fake `nix`. Each refusal is a negative
# control with its expected reason.
set -uo pipefail
source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/lib/gate_env.sh" || exit 2
ROOT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../.." && pwd)"
cd "$ROOT_DIR" || exit 2
for f in fetch.sh run.sh ci_check.sh lib.sh smoke.con; do
  [ -f "scripts/oracle/$f" ] || { echo "FATAL: scripts/oracle/$f missing" >&2; exit 2; }
done
TMP="$(mktemp -d)" || exit 2
trap 'rm -rf "$TMP"' EXIT
PASS=0; FAIL=0
ok(){ echo "  ok   $1"; PASS=$((PASS+1)); }
no(){ echo "  FAIL $1"; FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); }
has(){ case "$1" in *"$2"*) return 0;; esac; return 1; }

COMMIT=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111
mkdir -p "$TMP/oracle" "$TMP/bin" "$TMP/art"
cp scripts/oracle/fetch.sh scripts/oracle/run.sh scripts/oracle/ci_check.sh scripts/oracle/lib.sh \
   scripts/oracle/smoke.con "$TMP/oracle/"
# shellcheck source=scripts/oracle/lib.sh
. "$TMP/oracle/lib.sh"

# A test artifact in the real format: bin/concrete, std/, shell/, MANIFEST.sha256 (oracle_pack).
stage() {  # stage DIR BINARY_TEXT
  mkdir -p "$1/bin" "$1/std" "$1/shell"
  printf '#!/bin/sh\n# %s\nexit 0\n' "$2" > "$1/bin/concrete"; chmod +x "$1/bin/concrete"
  printf 'mod std;\n' > "$1/std/lib.con"
  printf '{ }\n' > "$1/shell/flake.nix"; printf '{}\n' > "$1/shell/flake.lock"
  printf 'leanprover/lean4:v4.34.1\n' > "$1/shell/lean-toolchain"
}
stage "$TMP/good" "the test oracle"
oracle_pack "$TMP/good" "$TMP/art/good.tar.gz" || { echo "FATAL: oracle_pack failed" >&2; exit 2; }
GOOD_SHA="$(sha256sum "$TMP/art/good.tar.gz" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
MAN_SHA="$(sha256sum "$TMP/good/MANIFEST.sha256" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
BIN_SHA="$(sha256sum "$TMP/good/bin/concrete" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
# An artifact that unpacks but whose manifest is not the locked one (another std file).
stage "$TMP/bad" "the test oracle"; printf 'mod other;\n' > "$TMP/bad/std/lib.con"
oracle_pack "$TMP/bad" "$TMP/art/badman.tar.gz" || { echo "FATAL: oracle_pack failed" >&2; exit 2; }
BADMAN_SHA="$(sha256sum "$TMP/art/badman.tar.gz" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
printf 'not the artifact\n' > "$TMP/art/other.bin"

write_lock() {  # write_lock URL ARTIFACT_SHA
  cat > "$TMP/oracle/ORACLE.lock" <<EOF
tag=test-tag
commit=$COMMIT
platform=x86_64-linux
binary_sha256=$BIN_SHA
manifest_sha256=$MAN_SHA
artifact_sha256=$2
artifact_url=$1
EOF
}
URL=https://example.invalid/oracle-test-tag-x86_64-linux.tar.gz

# The fake curl serves $FAKE_SERVE to -o, or fails when FAKE_SERVE is empty.
cat > "$TMP/bin/curl" <<'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
out=""; while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do [ "$1" = -o ] && { out="$2"; shift; }; shift; done
[ -n "${FAKE_SERVE:-}" ] || { echo "curl: (6) Could not resolve host" >&2; exit 6; }
cp "$FAKE_SERVE" "$out"
EOF
chmod +x "$TMP/bin/curl"

H="$TMP/home"
fetch() { rm -rf "$H"; PATH="$TMP/bin:$PATH" ORACLE_HOME="$H" FAKE_SERVE="${1:-}" bash "$TMP/oracle/fetch.sh" 2>&1; }


exec
/bin/bash -lc "sed -n '1,95p' docs/SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS.md; sed -n '95,170p' docs/SELF_HOSTED_RUNNERS.md; sed -n '1,100p' docs/LANDING.md; sed -n '378,440p' docs/LANDING.md; rg -n 'remote|repository|mirror|lambdaclass' docs/proposals/SPEC_UNIFICATION.md docs/decisions.md; nl -ba scripts/push-both.sh | sed -n '49,96p'; nl -ba scripts/checks/landing_script.sh | sed -n '725,750p'" in /tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-so-b/src
